%N A401272 a(n) is the smallest abundant number that is equal to the sum of n distinct abundant numbers (A005101).
%C A401272 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} A005101(k) = A173107(n) for n <> 3, 4, 13, 17, 18, 22, 23, ...
%C A401272 What is the least odd term?
%C A401272 Тhe sum of the first 277 abundant numbers equals 159075, with sigma(159075) = 328848, so the least odd term is <= 159075. - _Ivan N. Ianakiev_, Oct 28 2026
%e A401272 a(3) = 54 since A005101(10) = 54 and 54 = A005101(1) + A005101(2) + A005101(4) = 12 + 18 + 24 while A005101(1) + A005101(2) + A005101(3) = 12 + 18 + 20 = 50 is not an abundant number.
%Y A401272 Cf. A005101, A173107.
%K A401272 nonn,changed
%O A401272 1,1
